---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Cloud availability — WATeamInbox"
  description="WATeamInbox is open source and self-hostable. A managed Cloud option is planned, but no pricing, launch date, or service level has been announced."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs font-bold uppercase text-primary-700">
      Cloud status / plain language
    </p>
    <h1
      class="mt-4 max-w-3xl font-serif text-5xl font-medium leading-none text-slate-950 sm:text-6xl"
    >
      There is no hosted pricing to sell today.
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-8 text-slate-600">
      WATeamInbox is an open-source, self-hostable project. WATeamInbox Cloud is
      a planned managed option, and the waitlist only records interest after
      email confirmation.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-14 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2">
      <article
        class="border border-slate-300 bg-white p-8 shadow-[6px_6px_0_#dfe7dc]"
      >
        <p class="font-mono text-xs font-bold uppercase text-primary-700">
          Available now
        </p>
        <h2 class="mt-4 font-serif text-3xl font-medium text-slate-950">
          Self-hosted
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-slate-600">
          Use the MIT-licensed repository and operate the stack on
          infrastructure you control. Your hosting, backups, and deployment
          choices stay yours.
        </p>
        <a
          href="/docs"
          class="mt-7 inline-flex border-b border-primary-700 pb-1 font-mono text-sm font-bold text-primary-800 hover:text-primary-600"
          >Read deployment docs <span class="ml-1" aria-hidden="true">↗</span
          ></a
        >
      </article>
      <article
        class="border border-emerald-900 bg-emerald-950 p-8 text-emerald-50 shadow-[6px_6px_0_#bfd7bf]"
      >
        <p class="font-mono text-xs font-bold uppercase text-emerald-300">
          Future option
        </p>
        <h2 class="mt-4 font-serif text-3xl font-medium">WATeamInbox Cloud</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-emerald-100/80">
          We are collecting double-opt-in interest from teams that would prefer
          a managed service. No price, release date, feature set, or service
          level is promised yet.
        </p>
        <a
          href="/#waitlist"
          class="mt-7 inline-flex border-b border-emerald-200 pb-1 font-mono text-sm font-bold text-emerald-50 hover:text-emerald-200"
          >Join the waitlist <span class="ml-1" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
        >
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-14 border-t border-slate-200 pt-10">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-medium text-slate-950">
        What joining means
      </h2>
      <ul class="mt-6 grid gap-4 text-slate-600 sm:grid-cols-3">
        <li class="border-l-2 border-primary-600 pl-4">
          We send a confirmation email first.
        </li>
        <li class="border-l-2 border-primary-600 pl-4">
          Confirmed addresses count as demand for a managed option.
        </li>
        <li class="border-l-2 border-primary-600 pl-4">
          Joining does not create an account or a billing commitment.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
